  "body": "## Summary \n\nThe `DistributionCreator` contract lacks validation to ensure that campaign start timestamps are reasonable (example : `startTimestamp >= block.timestamp`). This allows users to create campaigns with past start times, including campaigns that have already completely ended before creation\n\n## Description\n\nIn the `_createCampaign` function, there is no validation check for the `startTimestamp` parameter:\n\nwhere the function as : \n\n```\nfunction _createCampaign(CampaignParameters memory newCampaign) internal returns (bytes32) {\n    // Validates duration\n    if (newCampaign.duration < HOUR) revert Errors.CampaignDurationBelowHour();\n    // Validates token whitelist\n    if (rewardTokenMinAmount == 0) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTokenNotWhitelisted();\n    // Validates minimum reward amount\n    if ((newCampaign.amount * HOUR) / newCampaign.duration < rewardTokenMinAmount) revert Errors.CampaignRewardTooLow();\n    \n    // missing: No validation for startTimestamp\n    // Should have: if (newCampaign.startTimestamp < block.timestamp) revert Errors.InvalidStartTime();\n}\n```\n\nfunction allows creating campaigns that already started or even fully elapsed (as long as duration >= 1 hour). This can create campaigns that have effectively ended at creation time; while the distributor/engine may ignore, the contract itself charges fees and stores the campaign.\n\n## impact \n\nUsers pay full fees and token amounts for campaigns that can never distribute rewards\n\n\n## Fix\n\nConsider enforcing `startTimestamp + duration > block.timestamp` or at least `startTimestamp >= block.timestamp` to prevent funding dead campaigns.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity \n\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: BUSL-1.1\n\npragma solidity ^0.8.17;\n\nimport {Test, console}  from \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\nimport {ERC20Mock} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/mocks/token/ERC20Mock.sol\";\nimport {DistributionCreator} from \"../../src/DistributionCreator.sol\";\nimport {DistributionParameters} from \"../../src/struct/DistributionParameters.sol\";\nimport { RewardTokenAmounts } from \"../../src/struct/RewardTokenAmounts.sol\";\nimport { CampaignParameters } from \"../../src/struct/CampaignParameters.sol\";\nimport {Distributor} from \"../../src/Distributor.sol\";\nimport {IAccessControlManager} from \"../../src/interfaces/IAccessControlManager.sol\";\nimport {ERC1967Proxy} from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/proxy/ERC1967/ERC1967Proxy.sol\";\n\ncontract MockAccessControlManager is IAccessControlManager {\n    function isGovernor(address) external pure returns (bool) {\n        return true;\n    }\n    \n    function isGovernorOrGuardian(address) external pure returns (bool) {\n        return true;\n    }\n}\n\ncontract testDistributionCreator is Test {\n    ERC20Mock RewardToken;\n    DistributionCreator distributionCreator;\n    Distributor distributor;\n    //address \n    address siddhu = makeAddr(\"siddhu\");\n    address alice = makeAddr(\"alice\");\n\n    address Governor = address(this);\n    MockAccessControlManager accessControlManager;\n\n    uint32 public constant HOUR = 3600; // 1 * 60 * 60\n\n    ///(represents 100%)\n    uint256 public constant BASE_9 = 1e9;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        RewardToken = new ERC20Mock();\n        accessControlManager = new MockAccessControlManager();\n\n        // Deploy implementation contracts\n        DistributionCreator distributionCreatorImpl = new DistributionCreator();\n        Distributor distributorImpl = new Distributor();\n        \n        // Deploy proxies and initialize\n        distributionCreator = DistributionCreator(address(new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(distributionCreatorImpl),\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(\n                DistributionCreator.initialize.selector,\n                accessControlManager,\n                address(distributorImpl),\n                1e2\n            )\n        )));\n        \n        distributor = Distributor(address(new ERC1967Proxy(\n            address(distributorImpl),\n            \"\"\n        )));\n        \n        RewardToken.mint(siddhu,100 ether);\n        vm.prank(siddhu);\n        RewardToken.approve(address(distributionCreator), type(uint256).max);\n    }\n\n    function test_alreadyInit() public {\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        distributionCreator.initialize(IAccessControlManager(accessControlManager), address(distributor), 1e2);\n    }\n\n\n    \n    function test_createCampaignAlreadyEnded() public {\n        // Whitelist the reward token first\n        address[] memory tokens = new address[](1);\n        uint256[] memory amounts = new uint256[](1);\n        tokens[0] = address(RewardToken);\n        amounts[0] = 1e12; // minimum amount per epoch\n        distributionCreator.setRewardTokenMinAmounts(tokens, amounts);\n        \n        // Warp to a future time to avoid underflow\n        vm.warp(block.timestamp + 10000);\n        \n        // Record initial balances\n        uint256 initialUserBalance = RewardToken.balanceOf(siddhu);\n        uint256 initialContractBalance = RewardToken.balanceOf(address(distributionCreator));\n        // Get the actual distributor address from the contract\n        address actualDistributor = distributionCreator.distributor();\n        uint256 initialDistributorBalance = RewardToken.balanceOf(actualDistributor);\n        \n        // Create campaign that already ended (started 2 hours ago, duration 1 hour)\n        uint32 pastTimestamp = uint32(block.timestamp - (HOUR * 2));\n        \n        CampaignParameters memory endedCampaign = CampaignParameters({\n            campaignId: bytes32(0),\n            creator: siddhu,\n            rewardToken: address(RewardToken),\n            amount: 1 ether,\n            campaignType: 1,\n            startTimestamp: pastTimestamp,\n            duration: HOUR, // 1 hour duration - already ended\n            campaignData: \"\"\n        });\n        \n        vm.prank(siddhu);\n        // This should succeed but creates a campaign that already ended\n        bytes32 campaignId = distributionCreator.createCampaign(endedCampaign);\n        \n        // Verify the campaign was created but already ended\n        CampaignParameters memory createdCampaign = distributionCreator.campaign(campaignId);\n        assertTrue(createdCampaign.startTimestamp + createdCampaign.duration < block.timestamp);\n        \n        // Check that fees were charged and tokens transferred despite campaign being dead\n        uint256 finalUserBalance = RewardToken.balanceOf(siddhu);\n        uint256 finalContractBalance = RewardToken.balanceOf(address(distributionCreator));\n        uint256 finalDistributorBalance = RewardToken.balanceOf(actualDistributor);\n        \n        // User lost tokens (paid for dead campaign)\n        assertTrue(finalUserBalance < initialUserBalance);\n        \n        // Tokens were transferred to distributor (wasted)\n        assertTrue(finalDistributorBalance > initialDistributorBalance);\n        \n        // Fees may have been kept in contract or sent to fee recipient\n        // Either way, the user paid for a campaign that can never distribute rewards\n        uint256 totalTokensSpent = initialUserBalance - finalUserBalance;\n        assertEq(totalTokensSpent, 1 ether); // User paid full amount for useless campaign\n        \n// Debugs\n        console.log(\"User paids:\", totalTokensSpent);\n        console.log(\"Feas kept in contract:\", finalContractBalance - initialContractBalance);\n        console.log(\"Tokens sent to distributors:\", finalDistributorBalance - initialDistributorBalance);\n        console.log(\"Campaign ended at:\", createdCampaign.startTimestamp + createdCampaign.duration);\n        console.log(\"Current time:\", block.timestamp);\n        console.log(\"Campaign was dead for almost :\", block.timestamp - (createdCampaign.startTimestamp + createdCampaign.duration), \"seconds\");\n    }\n\n\n}\n\n\n```\n\n> save it and run as : `❯ forge test --mt test_createCampaignAlreadyEnded -vvvv`",
